    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/055E28882001FE667534B0880CFCD275/jobs/96220": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Director Strategic Communications",
      "description": "Assistant Athletic Director Strategic Communications You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Athletic Director Strategic Communications Hot Job Jersey City, NJ 07306 Apply Overview Salary Range $50,000.00 - $52,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Apply Description About Saint Peter’s University Saint Peter’s is one of 27 Jesuit colleges and universities in the United States. Established in 1872, the University blends a unique learning experience shaped by rigorous academics, internships that provide real-world experience, community service, and a genuine, caring community that supports alumni long after graduation. Saint Peter’s offers more than 50 undergraduate majors as well as master’s level and doctorate programs. Saint Peter’s University’s diverse campus community, collegial and inclusive culture, and commitment to excellence, education, innovation and community engagement contribute to our success and ensures our employees flourish. The University merges quality academics, distinguished and exceptional faculty and staff, and modern facilities to engage and challenge its 4,000 students who share in the desire to shape the future through insight, intellectual exploration, discernment, and community service and engagement. Summary Description: Saint Peter’s University Athletics is seeking highly motivated applications for the position of Assistant AD for Strategic Communications. The incumbent will serve as a dynamic thought leader within athletics department, overseeing all aspects of media relations, public relations and communications. He/she will oversee the strategic development and execution of content dissemination across all platforms, including web, digital, print, external news platforms and social media. The position focuses on aligning departmental public relations and athletics communications with marketing, ticketing, fundraising and recruiting initiatives. The incumbent will oversee day-to-day operations of the athletics communications department, including creating consistency among brand channels to ensure appropriate tone and voice in all communications, promotions, and marketing pieces. This position reports to the Associate AD for Digital Media & Communications. Duties and Responsibilities: Develop and implement a comprehensive multi-media plan to showcase programs, student-athletes, and events that will enhance the Athletics department and University brand reputation through a comprehensive approach to public relations and media. Deliver the Saint Peter’s Athletics’ internal and external messaging and assist with marketing efforts to increase outreach and engagement with various constituent groups to enhance visibility of staff and student-athletes. Oversee a media relations/athletics communications plan for all sport programs while fostering productive relationships with local, regional, and national media outlets. Provide administrative leadership to full-time staff, graduate assistants, freelance and student staff/interns. Develop robust student athletics communications internship/practicum experiences for graduate assistant(s) and undergraduate students. Develop and plan work assignments for comprehensive coverage of all pertinent areas of communications and operations at home events, including the hiring and scheduling of stats crews/scoreboard/video board/operations support staff of select home events (soccer, volleyball, basketball, baseball, softball). Serve as the primary media contact for select sports, including men’s basketball. Assist in the production of digital marketing collateral and disseminate that content across all applicable platforms in a manner and voice consistent the department’s emphasis on instilling pride within all applicable audiences, in particular current and prospective student-athletes, as well as recent alumni. Write and deliver articulate and grammatically sound press releases on tight deadlines. Oversee design and creation of departmental publications, including game day program, posters, schedule cards, special event notices, and alumni/advancement material as appropriate for various sports and special events. Coordinate the daily maintenance and development of the official Saint Peter’s Athletics website and assure rosters, schedules, record books, etc., are updated in a timely manner and/or upon request from coaches/staff. Write press releases and feature stories promoting the department and its student-athletes. Serve as department spokesperson for all media requests for coaches, student-athletes and staff. Oversee historical archives and assure all pertinent website content is updated within a reasonable turnaround time at the conclusion of each season, including but not limited to: coach/staff/student-athlete bios, schedule archives, record book updates, updating rosters, photo galleries, etc. Pitch story ideas for Saint Peter’s University teams and student-athletes and provide stories when requested. Coordinate and present media relations training for coaches and student-athletes In collaboration with University and Athletics administration, establish protocol and best practices to effectively respond to crisis situations. Coordinate with external operations and marketing to increase awareness, attendance, and revenue for ticketed athletics events. Collaborate with marketing department on content and calendar of promotions, online sales, digital ads, etc. Interact with other University departments to promote athletics. Perform other duties as necessary to build support for and add value to the objectives and goals of the University, department of Athletics, and Athletics Communication unit. Any other duty or responsibility assigned by the supervisor Salary Range: $50,000 - $52,000 Benefits: Along with a competitive salary, we provide a robust benefits package to support your health and future goals. Key Benefits Include: Paid Time Off: Paid holidays, personal days, vacation, and sick leave Health Coverage: Health insurance, dental insurance, and vision insurance Life Insurance: Employer-provided life insurance Life & Disability Insurance: Voluntary life and voluntary disability coverage Retirement Savings: 401(k) plan with Roth and Traditional options Tuition Remission: An attractive tuition remission policy for employees and their dependents Additional Perks: Employee Assistance Program (EAP), Voluntary Legal plan, FSA and more The well-being of our employees is a priority for our University, and we are committed to promoting your success and well-being. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Previous experience preferably, in communications or public relations, within a college athletic department or professional sports organization; Extensive technological proficiency including experience with Adobe Creative Suite software (including InDesign, Photoshop and Premiere), Microsoft Office, NCAA LiveStats, StatCrew, SIDEARM websites and other relevant software programs necessary to perform the job duties described; Strong background in writing, editing, and design; in all forms of digital media (websites, social, video, mobile); Knowledge of effective public relations and communications strategies as they relate to intercollegiate athletics; Demonstrated ability to establish effective goal-oriented relationships with student-athletes, coaches, staff, University colleagues, media, and community members; Strong organization skills and ability to take initiative, multi-task, and achieve a high level of productivity in a collaborative environment under time sensitive deadlines; Ability to travel with select teams, including men’s basketball; Understanding of evolving trends and best practices in college athletics and social & digital media/fan engagement Ability to work effectively with a variety of people and units, including various stakeholders in the athletic department and across the institution. Organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a dynamic environment. Commitment to community engagement, service, leadership development, or related work. Preferred Qualifications: Experience developing and maintaining community partnerships. Experience working directly with community-based organizations. Familiarity with service-learning, civic engagement, volunteer management, or leadership development programs. Education: Bachelor’s degree in Communications, Public Relations, Journalism, Digital Media or a related field. Experience: The ideal candidate has previously worked in a college athletics setting, preferably at the Division I level, with experience in communications, media/public relations, sports information, etc., in addition to any undergraduate or graduate school experience. Proficiency with sport statistics programs such as Stat Crew and NCAA LiveStats; experience managing one or more team or departmental social media accounts; graphic design/illustration skills and experience as a public address announcer for one or more sports is also a plus. Licenses: Must have a valid driver’s license in good standing. Working Conditions: Regular evening and weekend work is required depending on home athletics events (particularly men’s/women’s basketball, MAAC Championship events, etc.); Some work around holidays will be required; Some travel will be required, particularly with men’s basketball. Physical Requirements: Incumbent may be required to work outdoors for extended periods of time (i.e., soccer and baseball/softball home games); Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/055E28882001FE667534B0880CFCD275/jobs/96734": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Athletics for Sports Performance",
      "description": "Associate Director of Athletics for Sports Performance You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Associate Director of Athletics for Sports Performance Hot Job Jersey City, NJ 07306 Apply Overview Salary Range $80,000.00 - $85,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Apply Description About Saint Peter’s University Saint Peter’s is one of 27 Jesuit colleges and universities in the United States. Established in 1872, the University blends a unique learning experience shaped by rigorous academics, internships that provide real-world experience, community service, and a genuine, caring community that supports alumni long after graduation. Saint Peter’s offers more than 50 undergraduate majors as well as master’s level and doctorate program. Saint Peter’s University’s diverse campus community, collegial and inclusive culture, and commitment to excellence, education, innovation and community engagement contribute to our success and ensures our employees flourish. The University merges quality academics, distinguished and exceptional faculty and staff, and modern facilities to engage and challenge its 4,000 students who share in the desire to shape the future through insight, intellectual exploration, discernment, and community service and engagement. Position Title and Job Summary: The Associate Director of Athletics for Sports Performance reports to the Director of Athletics and serves as a member of the department’s senior management team. This position supervises and coordinates the University’s sports medicine services and strength and conditioning services for a 16-sport Division 1 athletics program competing in the Metro Atlantic Athletic Conference. This individual will also design and maintain the training room operation. Develops all healthcare, S-A welfare, emergency action and SOP procedures and policies as well as training room regulations. Develops the administrative policy for the sports medicine department in cooperation with the Director of Athletics. Serves as a member of the department’s senior management team. Supervises all operations of the training room and the strength and conditioning operations. Implements the systems of evaluation, injury prevention, management, rehabilitation, and tracking. In conjunction with the head team physician and/or Chief Medical Officer, oversees and manages contracts with health care providers. Provides leadership and manages the assignments of the athletic training staff; ensuring appropriate athletic training coverage at home and away athletic events in and out of season. The position is responsible for providing direct athletic training services to all programs to include: injury prevention, evaluation, management, and treatment of athletic injuries, short-term and long-term rehabilitation of athletic injuries, education and counseling of student-athletes, and athletics related health care administration in consultation with and under the supervision of the Chief Medical Officer, Team Physician(s) and other qualified medical personnel. Any other duty or responsibility assigned by the supervisor Salary Range: $80,000 - $90,000 Along with a competitive salary, we provide a robust benefits package to support your health and future goals. Benefits: Key Benefits Include: Paid Time Off: Paid holidays, personal days, vacation, and sick leave Health Coverage: Health insurance, dental insurance, and vision insurance Life Insurance: Employer-provided life insurance Life & Disability Insurance: Voluntary life and voluntary disability coverage Retirement Savings: 401(k) plan with Roth and Traditional options Tuition Remission: An attractive tuition remission policy for employees and their dependents Additional Perks: Employee Assistance Program (EAP), Voluntary Legal plan, FSA and more The well-being of our employees is a priority for our University, and we are committed to promoting your success and well-being. Qualifications Required Qualifications: The Associate Director for Sports Performance is responsible for supporting the philosophy, goals and mission of the University and the Department of Athletics as well as adherence to Departmental, University, MAAC and the NCAA policies and procedures. Candidate must have a clear understanding of NCAA rules and compliance regulations. Strong communication and interpersonal skills combined with the ability to interact with diverse groups. Commitment and sensitivity to the needs and dynamics of a culturally diverse student body. Creative, innovative and self-motivated individual with the ability to work creatively in an atmosphere of limited resources. Commitment and sensitivity to the Jesuit and Catholic ideals that form the mission of Saint Peter’s University; and willingness to integrate these ideals into all aspects of the Athletics Department. Organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a dynamic environment. Commitment to community engagement, service, leadership development, or related work. Preferred Qualifications: Experience developing and maintaining community partnerships. Experience working directly with community-based organizations. Familiarity with service-learning, civic engagement, volunteer management, or leadership development programs. Education: Master’s Degree required. Must be certified by the National Athletic Trainers’ Association Board of Certification (NATABOC). Experience: At least five years of full-time experience in intercollegiate athletics department in a supervisory role. Working Conditions: This position includes working nights and weekends in support of scheduled events as required. Physical Requirements: The position requires the ability to lift, carry, push, and move athletic training equipment and supplies weighing up to 50 pounds. The employee must be able to stand, walk, bend, kneel, crouch, and reach for extended periods while providing medical coverage for practices, competitions, and other athletic events. The position also requires the ability to respond quickly to on-field injuries, assist with the transportation of injured student-athletes when appropriate, and perform repetitive physical tasks associated with athletic training and sports medicine services. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/055E28882001FE667534B0880CFCD275/jobs/98717": {
      "title": "Assistant Men's & Women's Track and Field Coach Part-time",
      "description": "Assistant Men's & Women's Track and Field Coach Part-time You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Men's & Women's Track and Field Coach Part-time Hot Job Jersey City, NJ 07306 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.92 - $16.39 Hourly Position Type Part Time Apply Description About Saint Peter’s University Saint Peter’s is one of 27 Jesuit colleges and universities in the United States. Established in 1872, the University blends a unique learning experience shaped by rigorous academics, internships that provide real-world experience, community service, and a genuine, caring community that supports alumni long after graduation. Saint Peter’s offers more than 50 undergraduate majors as well as master’s level and doctorate program. Saint Peter’s University’s diverse campus community, collegial and inclusive culture, and commitment to excellence, education, innovation and community engagement contribute to our success and ensures our employees flourish. The University merges quality academics, distinguished and exceptional faculty and staff, and modern facilities to engage and challenge its 4,000 students who share in the desire to shape the future through insight, intellectual exploration, discernment, and community service and engagement. Job Summary: The Part-Time Assistant M. & W. Track and Field Coach supports the Head M. & W. Track and Field Coach in all aspects of operating a competitive NCAA Division I program, including recruiting, student-athlete development, academic oversight, and compliance. Duties and Responsibilities: Assist in planning and conducting practices and skill development sessions Support game/match preparation, scouting, and in-game coaching Recruit prospective student-athletes in compliance with NCAA regulations Monitor academic progress and promote student-athlete success Assist with film breakdown and performance analysis Participate in team travel and program operations Ensure adherence to NCAA, conference, and institutional policies Support camps, clinics, and community engagement initiatives Any other duty or responsibility assigned by the supervisor. Hourly Range: $15.92 - $16.39 Qualifications Qualification Standards: Collegiate playing and/or coaching experience preferred Knowledge of NCAA Division I recruiting regulations Strong organizational and communication skills Ability to work evenings, weekends, and travel Education: Bachelor’s Degree required Experience: Collegiate playing and/or coaching experience preferred Knowledge of NCAA Division I recruiting regulations Licenses: Must have a valid driver’s license in good standing. Working Conditions: All staff must adhere to NCAA, conference, and institutional rules and regulations. Physical Requirements: Part-time, seasonal/academic year appointment. Evening, weekend, and travel required. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
