    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/055E28882001FE667534B0880CFCD275/jobs/99309": {
      "title": "Transfer Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Transfer Admissions Counselor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Transfer Admissions Counselor Hot Job Jersey City, NJ 07306 Apply Overview Salary Range $24.72 - $27.47 Hourly Position Type Full Time Apply Description About Saint Peter’s University Saint Peter’s is one of 27 Jesuit colleges and universities in the United States. Established in 1872, the University blends a unique learning experience shaped by rigorous academics, internships that provide real-world experience, community service, and a genuine, caring community that supports alumni long after graduation. Saint Peter’s offers more than 50 undergraduate majors as well as master’s level and doctorate program. Saint Peter’s University’s diverse campus community, collegial and inclusive culture, and commitment to excellence, education, innovation and community engagement contribute to our success and ensures our employees flourish. The University merges quality academics, distinguished and exceptional faculty and staff, and modern facilities to engage and challenge its 4,000 students who share in the desire to shape the future through insight, intellectual exploration, discernment, and community service and engagement. Job Summary: Reporting to the Director of Undergraduate Admissions, the Transfer Admissions Counselor represents the University to prospective transfer students, returning students, their families, community college counselors, academic advisors, and other college-access partners in a variety of on- and off-campus settings. The Transfer Admissions Counselor is responsible for the recruitment, admission, re-enrollment, and enrollment of prospective transfer and returning students, developing relationships with community colleges and other transfer partners, and guiding students through the admissions process from initial inquiry through enrollment. Supervisory Responsibility: This position has no direct reports. Outcomes / Performance Measures: Primary Duties: Serve as the primary contact for prospective transfer and re-enrolling students, providing individualized guidance through the admissions and enrollment process, including application completion, transcript review, and next steps toward registration. Provides transfer evaluations of transcripts and documentation in accordance with institutional policies. Work with academic departments, CASE and enrollment services offices to ensure accurate evaluation and placement of transfer credits. Lead outreach efforts to assist former students seeking re-admission, providing advice and support to facilitate their successful return and degree completion. Conduct proactive outreach to prospective students through phone calls, email, text messaging, virtual appointments, events, and other recruitment initiatives. Remains current on University programs and offerings to ensure accurate and up to date information is being provided to prospective students and other members of the community. Processes the application-related materials and corresponding student records in Slate and Colleague in a time-sensitive manner with accuracy and a strong attention to detail, and facilitates the timely completion of applications. Participate in and represent the University at transfer fairs, community college visits, college nights, open houses, information sessions, admitted student events, and other recruitment programs. Utilizes a variety of software programs including but not limited to Colleague, Slate, Outlook, Word, Excel, Zoom and other related programs. Performs other duties as assigned. Any other duty or responsibility assigned by the supervisor. Hourly Range: $24.72 - $27.47 Benefits: Along with a competitive salary, we provide a robust benefits package to support your health and future goals. Key Benefits Include: Paid Time Off: Paid holidays, personal days, vacation, and sick leave Health Coverage: Health insurance, dental insurance, and vision insurance Life Insurance: Employer-provided life insurance Life & Disability Insurance: Voluntary life and voluntary disability coverage Retirement Savings: 401(k) plan with Roth and Traditional options Tuition Remission: An attractive tuition remission policy for employees and their dependents Additional Perks: Employee Assistance Program (EAP), Voluntary Legal plan, FSA and more The well-being of our employees is a priority for our University, and we are committed to promoting your success and well-being. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required Strong organizational skills, with an attention to detail and ability to process critical information in a timely manner. Strong interpersonal and communication skills with a student-centered approach Experience working within a CRM (Slate) and Student Information System (Colleague) Experience in a higher education setting, preferably in an academic setting or advisement, Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment Availability to occasionally work outside of normal hours, evenings and/or weekends in the performance of assigned responsibilities. Ability to travel when needed (minimal and within state). Valid driver’s license required Organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a dynamic environment. Commitment to community engagement, service, leadership development, or related work. Preferred Qualifications: Experience developing and maintaining community partnerships. Experience working directly with community-based organizations. Familiarity with service-learning, civic engagement, volunteer management, or leadership development programs. Work Schedule: Full-time; In addition to regular business hours, the person in this position must be able to be flexible around the needs of the University, which includes occasional evening and/or weekend hours. Disclaimer: This job description is intended to summarize the type and level of work performed by the incumbent and is not an exhaustive list of duties, responsibilities, and requirements. The University reserves the right to change, add, or reassign job duties or combine positions, or portions thereof, at any time. This job description is not an employment agreement or contract. This job description may be updated from time to time based on the needs of the University. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/055E28882001FE667534B0880CFCD275/jobs/99575": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant of Health Services",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Administrative Assistant of Health Services Hot Job Jersey City, NJ 07306 Apply Overview Salary Range $23.00 - $26.00 Hourly Position Type Full Time Apply Description About Saint Peter’s University Saint Peter’s is one of 27 Jesuit colleges and universities in the United States. Established in 1872, the University blends a unique learning experience shaped by rigorous academics, internships that provide real-world experience, community service, and a genuine, caring community that supports alumni long after graduation. Saint Peter’s offers more than 50 undergraduate majors as well as master’s level and doctorate program. Saint Peter’s University’s diverse campus community, collegial and inclusive culture, and commitment to excellence, education, innovation and community engagement contribute to our success and ensures our employees flourish. The University merges quality academics, distinguished and exceptional faculty and staff, and modern facilities to engage and challenge its 4,000 students who share in the desire to shape the future through insight, intellectual exploration, discernment, and community service and engagement. Job Summary: This position encompasses secretarial, technical, and operational coordination skills of considerable difficulty, involving independent judgment and a strong emphasis on customer service. The Administrative Assistant serves as the primary point of contact for the Health Services Department. Duties include performing general office functions, managing electronic health records (EHR) in PyraMed, overseeing department email communications, tracking student immunization compliance, and supporting campus events throughout the year. Thorough knowledge of department functions, privacy regulations (HIPAA/FERPA), and university policies is essential. Duties and Responsibilities: 1, Front Desk Operations & Customer Service Provide exceptional, high-touch customer service as the initial point of contact for students, visitors, parents, and campus partners. Greet visitors warmly, answer phone inquiries, and manage front desk operations with a high level of empathy, professionalism, and confidentiality. 2. Electronic Health Records & System Management Maintain, update, and audit student electronic health records and files accurately using the PyraMed system in strict accordance with privacy guidelines. Input patient intake data, update medical history documentation, and assist students with navigating the PyraMed student health portal. Prepare statistical data and record summaries for monthly and annual departmental reports. 3. Immunization Compliance & Outreach Actively track and monitor student immunization records in PyraMed to ensure compliance with university and state health requirements. Conduct continuous proactive outreach and follow-up with incoming and returning students to request, collect, and verify required health and immunization documentation. 4. Department Communication & Email Management Manage and monitor the primary Health Services email account, ensuring timely, professional, and clear responses to all incoming student and administrative inquiries. Compose routine correspondence and departmental notices while adhering to strict privacy regulations. 5. University Events & Campus Engagement Represent and support the Health Services Department at major university events throughout the calendar year (e.g., Student Orientation, Wellness Fairs, Move-In Weekends, and Vaccine Clinics). Assist with event planning, logistics, setup, and distribution of health and wellness educational materials. 6. General Office Support Schedule appointments for the clinical staff. Assist with maintaining inventory levels of medical and office supplies. Provide suitable assignments and day-to-day guidance to work-study student employees. Operate and maintain office equipment, ensuring related logs and documentation are kept up to date. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Any other duty or responsibility assigned by the supervisor. Hourly Range: $23.00 - $26.00 Benefits: Along with a competitive salary, we provide a robust benefits package to support your health and future goals. Key Benefits Include: Paid Time Off: Paid holidays, personal days, vacation, and sick leave Health Coverage: Health insurance, dental insurance, and vision insurance Life Insurance: Employer-provided life insurance Life & Disability Insurance: Voluntary life and voluntary disability coverage Retirement Savings: 401(k) plan with Roth and Traditional options Tuition Remission: An attractive tuition remission policy for employees and their dependents Additional Perks: Employee Assistance Program (EAP), Voluntary Legal plan, FSA and more The well-being of our employees is a priority for our University, and we are committed to promoting your success and well-being. Qualifications Required Qualifications: 2–5 years of secretarial or administrative office experience, preferably in a healthcare, medical clinic, or higher education setting Organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a dynamic environment. Commitment to community engagement, service, leadership development, or related work. Preferred Qualifications: Experience developing and maintaining community partnerships. Experience working directly with community-based organizations. Familiarity with service-learning, civic engagement, volunteer management, or leadership development programs. Education: High School Diploma required; Associate or Bachelor’s degree preferred. Experience: Hands-on experience with Electronic Health Record (EHR) systems—experience with PyraMed is strongly preferred. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Outlook), Google Drive, and shared inbox/calendar management. Working Conditions: Academic Year: On-campus presence required during regular operational hours throughout the academic year to support student care. Summer Schedule: Potential opportunities for hybrid or remote work flexibility during summer operating periods, subject to departmental approval and operational needs. Events: Occasional evening or weekend availability required to support scheduled university-wide events across the calendar year. Physical Requirements: Ability to sit or stand at a desk/reception station for extended periods while assisting students and using a computer. Occasional lifting and moving of light equipment, promotional materials, or medical supply boxes (up to 20 lbs) for university events and office setup. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/055E28882001FE667534B0880CFCD275/jobs/100106": {
      "title": "Coordinator for Retention and Academic Success",
      "description": "Coordinator for Retention and Academic Success You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Coordinator for Retention and Academic Success Hot Job Jersey City, NJ 07306 Apply Overview Salary Range $50,000.00 - $55,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Apply Description About Saint Peter’s University Saint Peter’s is one of 27 Jesuit colleges and universities in the United States. Established in 1872, the University blends a unique learning experience shaped by rigorous academics, internships that provide real-world experience, community service, and a genuine, caring community that supp orts alumni long after graduation. Saint Peter’s offers more than 50 undergraduate majors as well as master’s level and doctorate programs. Saint Peter’s University’s diverse campus community, collegial and inclusive culture, and commitment to excellence, education, innovation and community engagement contribute to our success and ensures our employees flourish. The University merges quality academics, distinguished and exceptional faculty and staff, and modern facilities to engage and challenge its 4,000 students who share in the desire to shape the future through insight, intellectual exploration, discernment, and community service and engagement. Job Summary: The Coordinator for Retention and Academic Success is a key member of the Academic Affairs division and serves as a primary support for student academic achievement and persistence. Reporting to the Dean of CASE, this position works collaboratively with students, faculty, and staff to develop strategies that promote student retention and overall academic success. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide comprehensive academic advising using academic management systems to guide students toward successful degree completion. Design and implement individualized academic plans aligned with the students personal and career aspirations. Coordinate academic placement testing and ensure compliance with institutional and state standards. Monitor students’ academic progress and coordinate early intervention initiatives for students identified as at-risk, fostering persistence and success. Oversee office student worker supervision Collect, analyze, and interpret student performance and engagement data to identify trends, forecast challenges, and inform retention strategies. Develop and manage digital outreach, marketing, and recruitment campaigns to promote advising services and increase student engagement. Represent the department at orientation programs, recruitment events, and retention initiatives, including occasional evening and weekend commissions Salary Range: $50,000 - $55,000 Benefits: Along with a c ompetitive salary, we provide a robust benefits package to support your health and future goals. Key Benefits Include: Paid Time Off: Paid holidays, personal days, vacation, and sick leave Health Coverage: Health insurance, dental insurance, and vision insurance Life Insurance: Employer-provided life insurance Life & Disability Insurance: Voluntary life and voluntary disability coverage Retirement Savings: 401(k) plan with Roth and Traditional options Tuition Remission: An attractive tuition remission policy for employees and their dependents Additional Perks: Employee Assistance Program (EAP), Voluntary Legal plan, FSA and more The well-being of our employees is a priority for our University, and we are committed to promoting your success and well-being. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a dynamic environment. Commitment to community engagement, service, leadership development, or related work. Additional Qualifications and Competencies: Proficiency in educational technology and academic platforms such as Colleague, EAB Navigate, Microsoft Office Suite, and communication/collaboration tools. Experience with data analysis, management, and reporting. Strong verbal and written communication and presentation skills. Experience advising students, particularly those with disabilities or from underrepresented backgrounds. Ability to identify student behavioral trends and communicate findings effectively. Commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion; demonstrated use of data to promote equitable student outcomes. Exceptional attention to detail and a strong commitment to accuracy and confidentiality. Ability to participate in occasional evening or weekend recruitment and retention events. Fluency in a language other than English is preferred. Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree in a related field required. Master’s degree in student affairs, higher education, data analytics, or business administration required. 1–3 years of related experience in academic advising, student support, or retention services Preferred Qualifications: Experience developing and maintaining community partnerships. Experience working directly with community-based organizations. Familiarity with service-learning, civic engagement, volunteer management, or leadership development programs. Working Conditions: This is a full-time, on-campus position. Must be able to perform the essential functions of the position with or without reasonable accommodation. Physical Requirements: This position requires the ability to sit for extended periods, use a computer and other office equipment, and communicate effectively in person and by telephone. The employee may occasionally need to stand, walk, bend, reach, and lift or carry office materials weighing up to 10 pounds. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/055E28882001FE667534B0880CFCD275/jobs/100437": {
      "title": "Nursing and Health Professions Dean",
      "description": "Nursing and Health Professions Dean You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Nursing and Health Professions Dean Hot Job Jersey City, NJ 07306 Apply Overview Salary Range $125,000.00 - $150,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Apply Description The Opportunity: Saint Peter’s University seeks an innovative, student-focused leader to serve as Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions. The Dean is a member of the Academic Affairs leadership team and Deans Council and serves as the chief academic and administrative officer of the School. The Dean serves as the intellectual leader of the School, fostering an environment in which teaching, scholarship, and service can flourish. The Dean is responsible for the quality and stewardship of academic programs; for managing the School’s organizational structure and human and fiscal resources; and for championing opportunities for School students, faculty, and staff, both internally and externally. Working in collaboration with other Deans and senior administrators, the Dean of Nursing and Health Professions supports and promotes the mission and values of the University. About Saint Peter’s University: Saint Peter’s is one of 27 Jesuit colleges and universities in the United States. Established in 1872, the University blends a unique learning experience shaped by rigorous academics, internships that provide real-world experience, community service, and a genuine, caring community that supports alumni long after graduation. Saint Peter’s offers more than 50 undergraduate majors as well as master’s level and doctorate programs. Saint Peter’s University’s diverse campus community, collegial and inclusive culture, and commitment to excellence, education, innovation and community engagement contribute to our success and ensures our employees flourish. The University merges quality academics, distinguished and exceptional faculty and staff, and modern facilities to engage and challenge its 4,000 students who share in the desire to shape the future through insight, intellectual exploration, discernment, and community service and engagement. Duties and Responsibilities: Develop and advance a forward-looking vision for the School. Ensure inclusive excellence in teaching across disciplines. Build and retain a pipeline of students for undergraduate and graduate programs in Nursing and Healthcare professions Oversee the academic progress of students within the School. Investigate, adjudicate, and resolve student academic problems and complaints. Recruit, hire, and retain excellent teacher-scholars. Ensure clear and fair assessment of faculty and staff. Support faculty and program development in a manner consistent with the University mission and values. Develop and oversee the School curriculum to meet the needs of students and the University. Regularly review, assess, and improve programs within the School. Oversee compliance with relevant disciplinary accreditation and licensure requirements. Manage human and financial resources to achieve the goals of the School and the University. Build and sustain relationships with Hospitals and Healthcare systems. Advocate on behalf of the School’s students, faculty, and staff internally and externally. Collaborate with other Deans and University administrators to explore and support interdisciplinary partnerships. Represent the School at the University, in the community, and at national and international meetings. Develop and enhance fundraising relationships with individuals, corporations, and foundations. Recruit and convene at least three times per year an Advisory Council. Advise the VPAA and other senior leadership on University policies and procedures. Any other duty or responsibility assigned by the supervisor. Salary Range: $125,000 - $150,000 Benefits: Along with a competitive salary, we provide a robust benefits package to support your health and future goals. Key Benefits Include: Paid Time Off: Paid holidays, personal days, vacation, and sick leave Health Coverage: Health insurance, dental insurance, and vision insurance Life Insurance: Employer-provided life insurance Life & Disability Insurance: Voluntary life and voluntary disability coverage Retirement Savings: 401(k) plan with Roth and Traditional options Tuition Remission: An attractive tuition remission policy for employees and their dependents Additional Perks: Employee Assistance Program (EAP), Voluntary Legal plan, FSA and more The well-being of our employees is a priority for our University, and we are committed to promoting your success and well-being. Qualifications Required Qualifications: A terminal degree in a field that allows for appointment as a member of the faculty of Nursing and Health Professions. Demonstrated excellence in teaching, scholarship, and academic service. A successful record of academic administrative leadership experience at the departmental level or above. Intellectual curiosity about the disciplines represented in the School and about high-impact experiential and online learning. Demonstrated commitment to fostering inclusive excellence in curriculum design and pedagogy; in scholarship and creative endeavor; in service and community engagement; and in student outcomes. Excellent communication skills. Proven experience managing personnel. Proven experience with academic program evaluation. Demonstrated commitment to shared governance and collaboration across disciplines. Experience in working with and responding to National Accreditation bodies. Demonstrated experience with fiscal planning and budget management/analytics. Disposition to listen, unite, and lead the School’s diverse students, faculty, and staff. Ability to lift and carry up to 40 pounds. Organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a dynamic environment. Commitment to community engagement, service, leadership development, or related work. Preferred Qualifications: Experience developing and maintaining community partnerships. Experience working directly with community-based organizations. Familiarity with service-learning, civic engagement, volunteer management, or leadership development programs. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/055E28882001FE667534B0880CFCD275/jobs/12774": {
      "title": "Adjunct of MPA",
      "description": "Adjunct of MPA You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct of MPA Jersey City, NJ 07306 Quick Apply Overview Salary Range $855.00 - $1,012.00 Commission Quick Apply Description About Saint Peter’s University Saint Peter’s is one of 27 Jesuit colleges and universities in the United States. Established in 1872, the University blends a unique learning experience shaped by rigorous academics, internships that provide real-world experience, community service, and a genuine, caring community that supports alumni long after graduation. Saint Peter’s offers more than 50 undergraduate majors as well as master’s level and doctorate programs Duties and Responsibilities: The course focuses on models, qualities and characteristics of management and leadership within the public and non-profit sectors. Students will explore concepts of strategic management, team building, shared vision, pluralism, empowerment, agenda setting, and human resource management. Central to this class is the examination of how disputes are resolved from the perspectives of management, law, government, media, labor and the public. Rank: Adjunct Lecturer Tenure Information: Non-Tenure Track Adjunct Rate: $855 – $1,012 per credit Qualifications Qualification Standards: Must be detail oriented, creative, and organized Must possess excellent written and verbal communication skills Demonstrated excellence in teaching adult learners preferred Education: Candidates should have a Masters or PhD Degree in Public Administration, Management, or a related field. Experience: Experience working with a non-profit or public organization in management or conflict resolution, preferred. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/055E28882001FE667534B0880CFCD275/jobs/12770": {
      "title": "Adjunct of Political Science",
      "description": "Adjunct of Political Science You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct of Political Science Jersey City, NJ 07306 Quick Apply Overview Salary Range $840.00 - $900.00 Commission Quick Apply Description About Saint Peter’s University Saint Peter’s is one of 27 Jesuit colleges and universities in the United States. Established in 1872, the University blends a unique learning experience shaped by rigorous academics, internships that provide real-world experience, community service, and a genuine, caring community that supports alumni long after graduation. Saint Peter’s offers more than 50 undergraduate majors as well as master’s level and doctorate programs Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Political Science at Saint Peter’s University invites applications for a part- time faculty position specializing in American politics beginning in the fall of 2024. The successful candidate will be expected to teach a wide variety of American politics courses, including the department introductory political science course, basic American government course, as well as upper-level courses on Congress, the presidency, the courts, elections, and constitutional law. Rank: Adjunct Instructor Tenure Track: Non-Tenure Track Salary Range: $840 – $900 per credit. Qualifications Qualification Standards: The successful candidate must be available to teach during the day on either a Monday/Wednesday/ Thursday patters or a Tuesday/Friday pattern, and or in the evening, or online. Education: A minimum of a master’s degree (or higher) in political science is required. Experience: Applicants with studies in International Relations or Comparative Politics are preferred. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
