udent- centered learning experiences, helping students to connect concepts across the curriculum • Facilitate student engagement through the use of online tools and the features of the Blackboard LMS • Maintain an online presence to actively engage students, motivate them to succeed, and convey a genuine interest and enthusiasm for their learning and achievements • Assess student’s work, providing continuous constructive feedback advise students on improvements, support development with program and course objectives as a guide • Developing and implement appropriate assessments with the Program Director to evaluate course and program student learning outcomes and curricular goals • Maintain communication with the Program Director, identifying any students of concern and relaying student progress and provide feedback to the Program Director on possible curricular improvements Rank: Adjunct Instructor Tenure Information: Non-Tenure Track Rate per credit: $900 - $1,100 Qualifications Qualification Standards: Required: • Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills • Commitment to and experience in teaching health science courses • Experience teaching online • Experience working with students from a wide range of disciplines, cultures, academic, and professional backgrounds Desired: • Demonstrable scholarship in the health sciences, or closely related areas • Experience with mentorship of graduate students • Experience with Blackboard or similar LMS • Experience with teleconferencing software, particularly Zoom and Google Meet • Evidence of active participation in professional associations with an emphasis on healthcare leadership, community health, and/or health education Education: Master’s degree required, PhD. Preferred in Health Science, public health, or a closely related field. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
